 # Procedural Tree Voxel Generation
 
-Also called: L-system-like recursion, Recursive Tree Branching, Tree Voxel Generation, branch
+Also called: L-system-like recursion, L-systems, Lindenmayer systems, Recursive Tree Branching, Tree Voxel Generation
 
 ## Overview
-Procedural Tree Voxel Generation is a recursive algorithm that constructs tree structures by drawing tapered branches as sequences of spheres and spawning sub-branches at intermediate points [S1, unofficial]. It differs from its parent, [Sine-based procedural voxel generation](2477-sine-based-procedural-voxel-generation.md), by introducing hierarchical branching logic and variable thickness, rather than relying solely on periodic functions for shape definition [G]. It is distinct from [Simple Heightmap Voxel Generation](4649-simple-heightmap-voxel-generation.md) which generates terrain, and [Asymmetric Wing Stroke](5094-asymmetric-wing-stroke.md) which generates aerodynamic surfaces [G].
+Procedural Tree Voxel Generation is a method for creating volumetric tree structures by recursively branching segments represented as spheres of varying thickness [S1, unofficial]. It adapts L-system principles to voxel space, where a single recursive rule generates complex, self-similar shapes by spawning sub-branches with random directional offsets and scaling factors [S2, unofficial]. Unlike shape grammars that output basic shapes directly, this method requires interpreting the recursive production rules to draw voxelized primitives [S2, unofficial]. It is distinguished from sibling methods like Simple Heightmap Voxel Generation by its hierarchical, branching topology rather than surface elevation, and from Asymmetric Wing Stroke by its focus on organic, fractal-like growth patterns [S2, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
+
+### Inputs and Outputs
 **Inputs:**
-- `root1`: Start position of the branch (vec3) [S1, unofficial].
-- `root2`: End position of the branch (vec3) [S1, unofficial].
-- `thicknessA`: Radius at `root1` (float) [S1, unofficial].
-- `thicknessB`: Radius at `root2` (float) [S1, unofficial].
-- `iteration`: Current recursion depth (int) [S1, unofficial].
-- `iM`: Integer index for detail sphere offsets (int) [S1, unofficial].
+- `root1`: Starting 3D position (vector).
+- `root2`: Ending 3D position (vector) of the current segment.
+- `thicknessA`: Radius of the sphere at `root1`.
+- `thicknessB`: Radius of the sphere at `root2`.
+- `iteration`: Current recursion depth (integer).
+- `vx, vy, vz`: Dimensions of the voxel grid.
+- `voxel`: Bit-packed array storing occupancy.
+- `voxel_col1, voxel_col2`: Arrays storing color data.
 
 **Outputs:**
-- Voxel grid updates: Sets bits in the global voxel array corresponding to the branch geometry [S1, unofficial].
-- Recursive calls: Generates sub-branches [S1, unofficial].
